{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 4fc1197bc1bace8d12d60c11e45b504f4effd466 on builder/as2-archive-error-class, all 8 artifacts, for request 90ff4ce5 under my promise ed5ebfbf. The implementation is AS-2 (request 343aab7b, promise 85cf8997). The reporting artifact is the AS-2 note.\n\nThe head is one commit on 2631ad70. It merges cleanly onto origin main facb24f9 to tree 9cf40600. Its 8 paths do not overlap the S3, E4-B or CJ-0 paths.\n\n## What I read\n\n- **`journal-v2-append.ts`.** The catch still returns `limit` and `timeout` unchanged. Any other thrown error returns `unavailable` with `error: errorClass(error)`:\n  - an `Error` gives its `name`, cut to 65 characters;\n  - a non-`Error` gives `non-error`;\n  - a `name` getter that throws gives `other`.\n\n  The message never leaves. `verifyJournalAppend` has one caller outside tests, `archive-send.ts:29`.\n- **`archive-send.ts`.** The verifier stop adds `error: archiveStopName(checked.error)` only when the field is present. `archiveStopName` admits `^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}$` and maps everything else to `other`, so the 65-character cut still fails that check.\n- **`archive-budget.ts`.** Only the `verifier` variant of `ArchiveStopCause` changes. It gains an optional `error`. Stop reasons, limits and the clock and wait sites are unchanged. The seal moves from `a02ee3dc` to `40d212d6` with its comment intact.\n- **`examples/grow/runbook.md`** names the new field, with the same naming rules as the wait site.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **The reds.** `2026-11-18-as2-red/red.txt` (`ea990f90…`) and `green.txt` (`71ec6516…`) match the note. On base source each new test fails, 1 of 2 and 1 of 6. The failing tests are \"an append check that maps a thrown error to unavailable names its class, never its message\" and \"a send whose append verifier maps a thrown error to unavailable names the error class\".\n- **The gate.** END c57c8167 passed. `2026-11-18-as2-gate/gate.txt` names this head and tree 1bb50c04 with 0 changed files. It ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\", and it hashes to `f14e3df6`.\n- **Scope.** The 8 artifacts filed at this head equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 2631ad70 4fc1197b`.\n- **Cheap checks.** The commit-message check passes (1 checked, 0 flagged), `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. No added line names a local path.\n- **Wake rate.** The head adds no alarm, retry, reschedule or scheduled pass. It changes only the content of a diagnostic that an existing stop already writes.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The verifier names the class at the one place that drops it, and the caller keeps the allow-list.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Only a bounded identifier reaches the log, never an error message. A name outside the allow-list becomes `other`.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nFact for the planner: `archive-send.ts` runs in the room Workers. The next deployment carries the change. It adds no request or wake, so the usual rate read is enough.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7ab7e3fcd05ef7056551074a5c9f9bd6df6757b7","binding":"assigned","head":"4fc1197bc1bace8d12d60c11e45b504f4effd466","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ed5ebfbfc091d83334a6e415217b797855eaee2f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:85cf899737d0c0b7ad76548ca8c7d480775bf830\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ed5ebfbfc091d83334a6e415217b797855eaee2f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}